                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00/1091: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-13T13:00:00-03:00">November 13, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 13—noon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>158. Personal for the Under Secretary. I have been in informal communication with
                    the Catette since yesterday on the question of the President’s issuing a press
                    statement in regard to the Government’s alleged Rome-Berlin tendencies, et
                    cetera, et cetera. The President sent me word last night that he would issue
                    this afternoon a statement to the press denying those connections, et cetera, et
                    cetera.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
